 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Most modern laptops have swappable battery, so the first thing to get is a thin, light one with a good battery life. Look for one with five or six hours. A fold-down keyboard is worth the weight and a touchpad is much easier than a trackpad. Some laptops have a small touchpad built into the laptop, or a separate one that plugs in. The best of both is a laptop with a separate keyboard and a trackpad. Many laptops have a keyboard that folds down on top of the laptop. Look for one with a left-handed keyboard. It' the same as right-handed but the keys are switched around.",
